### installation de docker

REF: https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/debian/install-using-the-repository 

```sh
#!/bin/bash

# Add Docker's official GPG key:
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install ca-certificates curl gnupg
sudo install -m 0755 -d /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/debian/gpg | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg
sudo chmod a+r /etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg

# Add the repository to Apt sources:
echo \
  "deb [arch="$(dpkg --print-architecture)" signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/docker.gpg] https://download.docker.com/linux/debian \
  "$(. /etc/os-release && echo "$VERSION_CODENAME")" stable" | \
  sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/docker.list > /dev/null

# Install packages
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y docker-ce docker-ce-cli containerd.io docker-buildx-plugin docker-compose-plugin

sudo adduser theseus docker
newgrp docker

docker run hello-world
```

### activation du port serie sur Raspberry

```sh
sudo tee -a /boot/firmware/config.txt > /dev/null <<EOF
enable_uart=1
dtoverlay=uart0
dtoverlay=uart5
dtoverlay=disable-bt
EOF
```

enlever `console=serial0,115200` de `/boot/firmware/cmdline.txt`

```sh
sudo systemctl disable hciuart
sudo systemctl stop hciuart
```

### udev ports com

Valable pour les GPS WTRTK-982 et les LORA Heltec 32

```sh
sudo tee /etc/udev/rules.d/99-usb-devices.rules > /dev/null <<EOF
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="gps"
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", SYMLINK+="lora"
EOF
```

```sh
sudo udevadm control --reload
sudo udevadm trigger
```

## config GPS

### parametrage du WTRTK-982

```sh
pyserial-miniterm /dev/gps 115200
pyserial-miniterm /dev/ttyAMA0 115200
```

Config à envoyer au WTRTK-982 via le port ttyAMA0 de préférence
```sh
CONFIG COM2 9600
MODE ROVER
GPGGA COM2 1
GPRMC COM2 1
GPGSV COM2 1
GPGGA COM3 1
GPRMC COM3 1
GPGSV COM3 1
GPGSA COM3 1
SAVECONFIG
```

Référence:

* COM1: port usb mappé en /dev/gps sur le Raspberry
* COM2: connecté au lora
* COM3: mappé en Série sur /dev/ttyAMA0


### git clone du repo gps

```sh
git clone -b gps https://github.com/cbares/Ensea-CoHoMa-III-ROS.git gps

cp gps/.devcontainer/env.example .env

COMPOSE_BAKE=true docker compose -f gps/.devcontainer/docker-compose.gpsd-server.yaml build
docker compose -f gps/.devcontainer/docker-compose.gpsd-server.yaml up -d
```

### GPS RTK sur raspberry:
```sh
sudo apt install rtklib
```

```sh
str2str -in ntrip://crtk.net:2101/OUIL -out serial://ttyAMA0:115200:8:n:1
str2str -in ntrip://10.0.4.114:2101/ENSEA -out serial://ttyAMA0:115200:8:n:1
str2str -in tcpcli://10.0.4.114:2947#rtcm3 -out serial://ttyAMA0:115200:8:n:1
```

#### NTRIP Caster sur Server

La dernière version est nécessaire pour pouvoir caster en ntrip.

```sh
git clone git@github.com:rtklibexplorer/RTKLIB.git
cd RTKLIB && mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make str2str
cd ../bin

str2str -in ntrip://crtk.net:2101/OUIL -out ntripc://0.0.0.0:2101/ENSEA
```

## install meshstatic CLI

```sh
sudo apt install pipx && pipx install "meshtastic[cli]"
pipx ensurepath
sudo reboot
```

```sh
meshtastic --port /dev/lora --set position.rx_gpio 48 --set position.tx_gpio 47 --set position.gps_mode 1 --set position.broadcast_smart_minimum_interval_secs 1 --set position.broadcast_smart_minimum_distance 5 --set position.position_broadcast_smart_enabled true --set position.position_broadcast_secs 1 --ch-set module_settings.position_precision 32 --ch-index 0
```

